f pp.String:__Detailed_explanation_of_how_Bitcoin_mining_rewards_work_=PP+73480
'@PP+73480'CC String: "Detailed explanation of how Bitcoin mining rewards work"
f pp.String:__Rewards_in_this_app_are_generated_from_cloud_based_Bitcoin_mining_output_associated_with_your_total_plan_hashrate__e.g.__GH_s_or_TH_s__and_any_active_boosts._Mining_results_depend_on_real_Bitcoin_network_conditions__such_as_network_hashrate_difficulty__fees__and_uptime___so_rewards_vary_and_are_not_guaranteed._n_nPaid_plans_can_include_a_Continuity_Boost_that_starts_at_1___when_the_plan_begins_and_can_increase_over_time_while_the_plan_stays_active._Your_account_can_also_have_a_Loyalty_Boost_that_grows_as_you_obtain_free__rewarded__or_paid_plans._Your_in_app_rewards_may_be_multiplied_by_these_boosts_under_the_current_boost_rules__subject_to_change_._n_nFor_example__if_you_would_normally_receive_0.01_BTC_from_mining_output_credited_in_our_system__and_you_have_a_2___continuity_boost_on_your_plan_and_a_2___loyalty_boost_on_your_account__the_example_reward_would_be_multiplied_by_both_boosts__resulting_in_0.04_BTC_under_the_current_boost_settings._This_is_an_illustration_only_and_does_not_guarantee_any_specific_reward_amount_or_boosts._n_nOur_boost_rules__limits__and_reward_allocation_mechanics_may_be_updated_over_time_based_on_factors_such_as_Bitcoin_network_conditions_and_operational_constraints._As_a_result__rewards_can_be_higher_or_lower_from_day_to_day_and_are_never_guaranteed._n_nWe_provide_access_to_cloud_mining_through_plans_rather_than_assigning_you_ownership_of_specific_physical_mining_hardware._This_approach_can_let_us:_n____apply_continuity_and_loyalty_boosts_flexibly__n____run_limited_time_promotions_and_reward_events__and_n____manage_fraud_prevention__risk__and_operational_costs_while_keeping_the_experience_consistent._n_nMining_is_performed_using_cloud_based_infrastructure_and_or_mining_pool_services_that_we_operate_or_source_through_providers._In_some_cases__we_may_also_use_virtualization_to_keep_the_experience_consistent__for_example__during_maintenance__capacity_constraints__or_risk_controls_._You_are_not_directly_connected_to_specific_machines_or_pool_accounts__instead__rewards_are_credited_based_on_your_plan__s_hashrate_share_and_the_boost_mechanics_described_above._n_n_=PP+73472
'@PP+73472'CC String: "Rewards in this app are generated from cloud-based Bitcoin mining output associated with your total plan hashrate (e.g., GH/s or TH/s) and any active boosts. Mining results depend on real Bitcoin network conditions (such as network hashrate/difficulty, fees, and uptime), so rewards vary and are not guaranteed.\n\nPaid plans can include a Continuity Boost that starts at 1× when the plan begins and can increase over time while the plan stays active. Your account can also have a Loyalty Boost that grows as you obtain free, rewarded, or paid plans. Your in-app rewards may be multiplied by these boosts under the current boost rules (subject to change).\n\nFor example, if you would normally receive 0.01 BTC from mining output credited in our system, and you have a 2× continuity boost on your plan and a 2× loyalty boost on your account, the example reward would be multiplied by both boosts, resulting in 0.04 BTC under the current boost settings. This is an illustration only and does not guarantee any specific reward amount or boosts.\n\nOur boost rules, limits, and reward allocation mechanics may be updated over time based on factors such as Bitcoin network conditions and operational constraints. As a result, rewards can be higher or lower from day to day and are never guaranteed.\n\nWe provide access to cloud mining through plans rather than assigning you ownership of specific physical mining hardware. This approach can let us:\n• apply continuity and loyalty boosts flexibly,\n• run limited-time promotions and reward events, and\n• manage fraud prevention, risk, and operational costs while keeping the experience consistent.\n\nMining is performed using cloud-based infrastructure and/or mining pool services that we operate or source through providers. In some cases, we may also use virtualization to keep the experience consistent (for example, during maintenance, capacity constraints, or risk controls). You are not directly connected to specific machines or pool accounts; instead, rewards are credited based on your plan\'s hashrate share and the boost mechanics described above.\n\n"
f pp.String:__Help_screen_section_title_about_rewards_=PP+73464
'@PP+73464'CC String: "Help screen section title about rewards"
